  "title": "India's Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel Celebrates Birth Anniversary on National Unity Day",
  "summary": "President Droupadi Murmu paid tributes to Sardar Patel on his 151st birth anniversary, honoring his contributions to India's unity and independence. The event also saw BJP paying tribute to him, with Union Home Minister Amit Shah acknowledging his role in shaping modern India.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel was born in 1875 in Nadiad, Gujarat, and celebrated his 151st birth anniversary as National Unity Day.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The event included a tribute from President Droupadi Murmu and a post from the BJP, highlighting Patel's role in India's development and national unity.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The ceremony emphasized Patel's contributions as an architect of modern India and a symbol of national unity and integrity.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
