      "title": "President Murmu pays tribute to Sardar Patel on 151st birth anniversary",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/president-murmu-pays-tribute-to-sardar-patel-on-151st-birth-anniversary-126103100253_1.html",
      "description": "President Droupadi Murmu on Saturday paid tributes on the 151st birth anniversary of 'Iron Man' Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel and said his contribution as a leading warrior of the freedom struggle and a principal architect of modern India is unforgettable.\nHe played a historic role in the unification of the country and the establishment of a strong administrative system, she said in a post on X in Hindi.\nBorn in Nadiad, Gujarat, on this day in 1875, Patel was a pivotal figure in India's struggle for Independence. His birth anniversary is celebrated as National Unity Day.\n\"On the 151st birth anniversary of the 'Iron Man' Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel, I offer him my humble tributes. His contribution as a leading warrior of the freedom struggle and a principal architect of modern India is unforgettable,\" the president said.\nIn honour of his incomparable contribution to the unity and integrity of the nation, we observe his birth anniversary as 'National Unity Day', she said.\n\"It is my wish tha",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-31T06:07:55"
    },
    {
      "title": "National Unity Day: BJP pays tribute to Sardar Patel on birth anniversary",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/national-unity-day-bjp-pays-tribute-to-sardar-patel-on-birth-anniversary-126103100104_1.html",
      "description": "The BJP on Saturday paid tributes to Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel and his contribution to the country's unity and integrity on his birth anniversary, and extended greetings to people on the occasion of National Unity Day.\nIn a post on X, Union Home Minister Amit Shah described Patel as the architect of modern India and a symbol of national unity and integrity, saying the country's foundation was strengthened by his courage and foresight.\n\"With his indomitable courage and foresight, Sardar Sahab united a country divided into princely states and laid the foundation of a strong India and by establishing the All India Services, he provided a robust base to the country's administrative system,\" he said.\nHe also recalled Patel's struggle for farmers' rights through the Kheda and Bardoli Satyagrahas, describing it as an unparalleled example of public service and leadership.\nPatel's sacrifice, dedication and patriotism will continue to inspire every citizen towards building an \"Ek Bharat, ...",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-31T04:37:40"
    }
